<%
  page_title "Release Notes"
  page_description "What's new in insAIght Hub — new features, improvements, and fixes."
%>

<style>
  @keyframes release-shimmer { to { background-position: -200% 0; } }
  @keyframes release-pulse { 0%, 100% { opacity: 0.25; } 50% { opacity: 1; } }
  .release-shimmer {
    background: linear-gradient(100deg, var(--color-base-300) 40%, var(--color-base-200) 50%, var(--color-base-300) 60%);
    background-size: 200% 100%;
    animation: release-shimmer 1.4s infinite linear;
  }
  .release-dot { animation: release-pulse 1.2s infinite ease-in-out; }
  .release-dot:nth-child(2) { animation-delay: 0.15s; }
  .release-dot:nth-child(3) { animation-delay: 0.3s; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .release-shimmer, .release-dot { animation: none; }
  }
</style>

<div class="container mx-auto px-4 py-8 max-w-3xl">
  <div class="badge badge-primary badge-outline mb-4">Release Notes</div>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold mb-1">Notifications, endless browsing, and a faster, safer insAIght Hub</h1>
  <p class="text-base-content/60 mb-6">July 7, 2026</p>
  <p class="text-lg text-base-content/70 mb-10">A big couple of days for the Hub: your team's activity now finds you instead of the other way around, the Insights library scrolls forever, and the whole platform moved to the newest Rails with a clean security bill of health.</p>

  <!-- Notifications -->
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Notifications <span class="badge badge-primary badge-sm align-middle">New</span></h2>
    <p class="mb-3">You no longer have to check back to know what's happening. insAIght Hub now notifies you &mdash; in the app and by email &mdash; when the things you care about change:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1 mb-3">
      <li><strong>New insights</strong> &mdash; when a teammate publishes to your organization</li>
      <li><strong>Updates</strong> &mdash; when a published insight you follow gets revised</li>
      <li><strong>Comments</strong> &mdash; when someone comments on one of your insights</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-base-content/70 mb-6">The bell in the sidebar updates live &mdash; no refresh needed &mdash; and each channel (in-app, email) can be switched on or off independently from your <%= link_to "profile settings", edit_profile_path, class: "link link-primary" %>. Read notifications tidy themselves up automatically after 90 days.</p>

    <div class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300">
      <div class="card-body items-center py-10">
        <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
          <div class="mt-1 p-2.5 rounded-full bg-base-100 border border-base-300 shadow relative shrink-0">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-5 w-5 text-base-content/70" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M6 8a6 6 0 0 1 12 0c0 7 3 9 3 9H3s3-2 3-9"/><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" d="M10.3 21a1.94 1.94 0 0 0 3.4 0"/></svg>
            <span class="absolute -top-1 -right-1 w-4.5 h-4.5 min-w-[1.1rem] rounded-full bg-primary text-primary-content text-[0.65rem] font-bold flex items-center justify-center leading-none">2</span>
          </div>
          <div class="w-80 max-w-full bg-base-100 border border-base-300 rounded-2xl shadow-xl overflow-hidden text-sm">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between px-4 pt-3.5 pb-2.5">
              <span class="font-bold text-base">Notifications</span>
              <span class="text-primary text-xs font-medium">Mark all read</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 border-t border-base-300">
              <span class="w-9 h-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary/15 text-primary font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">MP</span>
              <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="leading-snug"><span class="font-semibold">Maria Park</span> <span class="text-base-content/70">published</span> <span class="font-semibold">Q3 Churn Deep-Dive</span></p>
                <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50 mt-0.5">12 minutes ago</p>
              </div>
              <span class="w-2 h-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" title="Unread"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 border-t border-base-300">
              <span class="w-9 h-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary/15 text-primary font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">DK</span>
              <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="leading-snug"><span class="font-semibold">Devon Kim</span> <span class="text-base-content/70">commented on</span> <span class="font-semibold">Onboarding Funnel Notes</span></p>
                <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50 mt-0.5">1 hour ago</p>
              </div>
              <span class="w-2 h-2 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-primary" title="Unread"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 px-4 py-3 border-t border-base-300 opacity-60">
              <span class="w-9 h-9 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-base-300 text-base-content/70 font-bold text-xs flex items-center justify-center">AL</span>
              <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
                <p class="leading-snug"><span class="font-semibold">Alex Liu</span> <span class="text-base-content/70">updated</span> <span class="font-semibold">Pricing Experiment Results</span></p>
                <p class="text-xs text-base-content/50 mt-0.5">Yesterday</p>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-3">The sidebar bell and its dropdown &mdash; unread marked with a dot, updating in real time.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Infinite scroll -->
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Endless browsing on the Insights page <span class="badge badge-primary badge-sm align-middle">New</span></h2>
    <p class="text-base-content/80 mb-6">Pagination is gone. The Insights library now loads continuously as you scroll &mdash; and it pre-loads the next batch well before you reach the bottom, so there's no pause and no "Next page" button to hunt for. Your audience, member, tag, and search filters all carry through as you go.</p>

    <div class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300">
      <div class="card-body items-center py-8">
        <div class="w-full max-w-md grid grid-cols-2 gap-3">
          <div class="bg-base-100 border border-base-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow">
            <div class="h-12" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#6c5ce7,#a29bfe)"></div>
            <div class="p-3"><p class="text-xs font-semibold leading-tight">Q3 Churn Deep-Dive</p><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-2"></div><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-base-100 border border-base-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow">
            <div class="h-12" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#00b894,#55efc4)"></div>
            <div class="p-3"><p class="text-xs font-semibold leading-tight">Onboarding Funnel Notes</p><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-2"></div><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-base-100 border border-base-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow">
            <div class="h-12" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#e17055,#fab1a0)"></div>
            <div class="p-3"><p class="text-xs font-semibold leading-tight">Pricing Experiment Results</p><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-2"></div><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-base-100 border border-base-300 rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow">
            <div class="h-12 release-shimmer"></div>
            <div class="p-3"><div class="h-2.5 rounded release-shimmer"></div><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-2"></div><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="col-span-2 flex justify-center gap-1.5 pt-2">
            <span class="release-dot w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span class="release-dot w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
            <span class="release-dot w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-primary"></span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-3">The next page of insights streams in before you reach the bottom.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- iOS shell -->
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">A native iOS shell <span class="badge badge-primary badge-sm align-middle">New</span></h2>
    <p class="text-base-content/80 mb-6">insAIght Hub can now run as a native iOS app. A proper tab bar puts Dashboard, Browse, and Profile one thumb-tap away, the layout respects the iPhone's safe areas, and links open where you'd expect. Notifications flow through here too &mdash; the badge on the bell stays live on mobile.</p>

    <div class="card bg-base-200 border border-base-300">
      <div class="card-body items-center py-8">
        <div class="w-60 bg-base-100 border border-base-300 rounded-3xl shadow-xl overflow-hidden">
          <div class="w-24 h-4 mx-auto mt-2 bg-neutral rounded-full"></div>
          <div class="p-4 pb-2">
            <p class="text-sm font-bold mb-3">Dashboard</p>
            <div class="border border-base-300 rounded-lg p-2.5 mb-2"><p class="text-xs font-semibold">Q3 Churn Deep-Dive</p><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
            <div class="border border-base-300 rounded-lg p-2.5 mb-2"><p class="text-xs font-semibold">Incident Response Runbook</p><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
            <div class="border border-base-300 rounded-lg p-2.5"><p class="text-xs font-semibold">Pricing Experiment Results</p><div class="h-1.5 rounded bg-base-300 mt-1.5 w-3/5"></div></div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex border-t border-base-300 pt-2 pb-4">
            <span class="flex-1 flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5 text-primary text-[0.6rem] font-semibold">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="m3 9 9-7 9 7v11a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2z"/><polyline points="9 22 9 12 15 12 15 22"/></svg>
              Dashboard
            </span>
            <span class="flex-1 flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5 text-base-content/60 text-[0.6rem] font-semibold">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M9 18h6"/><path d="M10 22h4"/><path d="M15.09 14c.18-.98.65-1.74 1.41-2.5A4.65 4.65 0 0 0 18 8 6 6 0 0 0 6 8c0 1 .23 2.23 1.5 3.5A4.61 4.61 0 0 1 8.91 14"/></svg>
              Browse
            </span>
            <span class="flex-1 flex flex-col items-center gap-0.5 text-base-content/60 text-[0.6rem] font-semibold">
              <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><circle cx="12" cy="8" r="5"/><path d="M20 21a8 8 0 0 0-16 0"/></svg>
              Profile
            </span>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-base-content/60 mt-3">Dashboard, Browse, and Profile as native tabs on iPhone.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Fixes -->
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Fixes you'll actually notice <span class="badge badge-success badge-outline badge-sm align-middle">Fixed</span></h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Links inside insights work again.</strong> Clicking an internal link within an insight no longer bounces you to the sign-in page &mdash; navigation inside multi-page insights is back to normal, on private and shared links alike.</li>
      <li><strong>Export downloads reliably.</strong> The Export action now triggers a proper file download every time.</li>
      <li><strong>Insight names are per-organization.</strong> Two organizations can now each have an insight with the same name without colliding.</li>
      <li><strong>Dashboard ordering.</strong> Recently updated insights now surface first, with a clear "updated" label.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <!-- Under the hood -->
  <section class="mb-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">Under the hood <span class="badge badge-ghost badge-sm align-middle">Improved</span></h2>
    <p class="mb-3">A full security audit and modernization pass, with zero behavior changes:</p>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Security patches across the stack</strong> &mdash; cleared every actionable advisory, including two high-severity issues in the web server and an update of the MCP SDK from <code class="bg-base-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">0.4</code> to <code class="bg-base-200 px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-sm">0.23</code>. Static analysis reports zero warnings.</li>
      <li><strong>Rails 8.1</strong> &mdash; the platform now runs the newest Rails with all of its updated framework defaults, including stricter redirect safety.</li>
      <li><strong>Real-time infrastructure</strong> &mdash; notifications ride on Solid Cable 4 with database-backed delivery in production.</li>
      <li><strong>Deeper test coverage</strong> &mdash; the MCP integration (how AI assistants read and write insights) is now covered by its own test suite, and the new infinite scroll ships with tests for every path.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <p class="text-base-content/60 text-sm border-t border-base-300 pt-6">Questions or something misbehaving? <a href="https://github.com/c-sonnier/insaight-hub/issues" class="link link-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Open an issue on GitHub</a> &mdash; updates apply automatically the next time your Hub restarts.</p>
</div>
